<%# What the patient declared about themselves, summarised — the OTHER half of
    the evidence. The verdict banner, score card and counts beside it read only
    values the centre recorded; without this a patient who reached Candidato on
    their own answers showed "0 cumplidos" next to the badge, with nothing on
    the page saying why they were a candidate at all (found 2026-10-06).

    Kept apart from those on purpose and never added to them: a declaration is
    testimony, enough for the triage step and never for the clinical one.
    Renders nothing when the patient declared nothing. Locals:
      result — the patient's self_report_result (an EligibilityResult over declarations), or nil
%>
<% if result && result.answered_count.positive? %>
  <div class="alert alert-info py-2 mb-3">
    <p class="mb-1">
      <i class="bi bi-chat-left-quote"></i>
      <strong><%= t("criteria_assessments.self_report.title") %></strong>
    </p>
    <ul class="mb-1 small">
      <% if result.basic_total_count.positive? %>
        <li><%= t("criteria_assessments.self_report.basic", met: result.basic_passing.count, total: result.basic_total_count) %></li>
      <% end %>
      <% if result.basic_failing.any? %>
        <li><%= t("criteria_assessments.self_report.basic_failing", count: result.basic_failing.count) %></li>
      <% end %>
      <% if result.specific_total_count.positive? %>
        <li><%= t("criteria_assessments.self_report.specific", met: result.specific_score, total: result.specific_total_count) %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-0 small text-muted">
      <%= t("criteria_assessments.self_report.note",
            candidate: t("patients.states.candidate"), potential: t("patients.states.potential")) %>
    </p>
  </div>
<% end %>
